        "page_index": 0,
        "markdown": "## Most of the consultancy industry's professionals hold university degrees (percentage in Spain)\n\n[Figure]\n\n[Figure]\n\nSource: AEC (Spanish Association of Consulting Firms)\n\nDue to the type of services offered, consulting firms attract the most qualified profiles in the job market. 65.8% of the total number of professionals in 2024 were university graduates.Another year again, the percentage of women with a higher education was above that of men (70.8% verSUS 63.8%).\n\nOn the other hand,the presence ofvocationaltraining graduates dropped with respect to the year before, representing 20.1% of the total in 2.24. In this case, the percentage of women, 13.9% of the total, was less than the men, which represented 22.9%.\n\n## University degree holders from STEM areas\n\n(percentage in Spain)\n\n[Figure]\n\n[Figure]\n\nDegree holders in STEM fields Degree holders in other fields\n\n[Figure]\n\nSource: AEC (Spanish Association of Consulting Firms)",
